1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,991
A paper-trading fill can look convincing.

2
00:00:01,991 --> 00:00:06,968
But it is not proof that a live order would have filled the same way.

3
00:00:06,968 --> 00:00:07,964
The gap matters.

4
00:00:07,964 --> 00:00:13,247
In Alpaca's paper environment, an order is not routed to a live exchange.

5
00:00:13,247 --> 00:00:16,498
The system simulates a fill using real-time quotes.

6
00:00:16,498 --> 00:00:23,001
That makes paper trading useful for testing code and workflow, but the result is still a

7
00:00:23,001 --> 00:00:23,407
simulation.

8
00:00:23,407 --> 00:00:29,344
The documentation lists important omissions: market impact, information leakage, price slippage

9
00:00:29,344 --> 00:00:35,820
caused by latency, queue position for non-marketable limit orders, price improvement, regulatory

10
00:00:35,820 --> 00:00:37,439
fees and dividends.

11
00:00:37,439 --> 00:00:41,217
Those effects can change a real outcome.

12
00:00:41,217 --> 00:00:42,829
There is another limitation.

13
00:00:42,829 --> 00:00:48,874
Order quantity is not checked against the displayed best bid and offer quantities, known as

14
00:00:48,874 --> 00:00:49,277
NBBO.

15
00:00:49,277 --> 00:00:55,321
A simulated order can receive a fill larger than the liquidity shown at that moment.

16
00:00:55,321 --> 00:00:58,948
Do not treat that as proof of real-world capacity.

17
00:00:58,948 --> 00:01:04,534
Different simulators may also use different fill prices, liquidity assumptions, return

18
00:01:04,534 --> 00:01:07,073
calculations and market data sources.

19
00:01:07,073 --> 00:01:12,151
Results from one environment do not automatically transfer to another.

20
00:01:12,151 --> 00:01:18,408
Keep a paper-trading journal that names the simulator, data source and assumptions.

21
00:01:18,408 --> 00:01:24,666
Test conservative costs and partial execution scenarios where your tools allow it.

22
00:01:24,666 --> 00:01:27,794
Separate simulated outcomes from live-money performance.

23
00:01:27,794 --> 00:01:33,530
Paper-trading education only; not live-money performance; not investment advice; no guaranteed

24
00:01:33,530 --> 00:01:34,051
returns.
